                <pb facs="0428" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/217.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial German Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In reply to your note of
                    the 29th instant, serial No. 470, I have the honor respectfully to say that I am
                    authorized by the Imperial Government to accept the amendments to the loan
                    agreement with Liberia as proposed in the aforesaid note.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
